\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces One execution of the corridor policy, as models. A double circle is a designated world; an edge labelled $i$ is agent $i$ being unable to tell the two apart. Sensing splits the model and drops the sensing agent's edge in each half --- only the blocked half is drawn --- and the announcement drops everyone else's. The mission is over when no edge is left, which is what $\mathit  {Kw}$ asks for.\relax }}{5}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:corridor-models}{{3}{5}{One execution of the corridor policy, as models. A double circle is a designated world; an edge labelled $i$ is agent $i$ being unable to tell the two apart. Sensing splits the model and drops the sensing agent's edge in each half --- only the blocked half is drawn --- and the announcement drops everyone else's. The mission is over when no edge is left, which is what $\Kw $ asks for.\relax }{figure.caption.9}{}}
